+
+## Composed repairs
+
+1. The eight correctness checks formerly written as Python `assert` statements are now
+   explicit fail-closed exceptions. Five were in `build_v3.py` (canonical digest,
+   archive digest, file count, source hashes, and `FILES.json`); three were in
+   `apply_v3.py` (exact-once anchors and duplicate configuration keys). The checks now
+   survive `python -O` and `PYTHONOPTIMIZE=1`.
+2. Configuration defaults are preflighted as one set before mutation. A lane or parameter
+   collision raises without partially adding any other V3 keys.
+3. `build_v3.py --tree` now accepts only canonical relative POSIX member names, rejects
+   symlink/file/non-empty destinations, stages every byte beside the target, reads the
+   staged tree back, and publishes with one rename. A write failure cannot leave a partial
+   candidate tree.
+
+The exact-tree logic is composed from SOL-CLEANROOM PR #11990, head
+`f0aa57e3550e88372703caa95dc9f1cdf3d61546`. The optimized-mode assertion audit was
+released in Slack at message `1789068591.968719`.
+
+## Verification contract
+
+Run from this directory:
+
+```bash
+python -B -m py_compile build_v3.py apply_v3.py test_build_v3_tree.py test_v3_optimization_hardening.py
+python -B -m unittest -v test_build_v3_tree.py test_v3_optimization_hardening.py
+PYTHONOPTIMIZE=1 python -B -m unittest -v test_build_v3_tree.py test_v3_optimization_hardening.py
+python -B build_v3.py --check
+python -B build_v3.py --tree /tmp/titan-v3-s17
+cd /tmp/titan-v3-s17
+python -B -m unittest -v checks/test_v3_features.py checks/test_v3_l01.py checks/test_v3_r01.py checks/test_v3_r02.py
+```
+
+The path-scoped workflow `.github/workflows/titan-v3-s17-optimization-safe-tree.yml`
+executes that full contract against the repository-resident canonical archive and verifies
+that the materialized tree exactly matches `FILES.json`.
